      "html": "<section class=\"ds-card\"><h2 class=\"ds-card-title\">Каналы устройства</h2><div class=\"ds-card-body\">Состояние устройства</div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-card{background:var(--content-background,#fff);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#e0e6df);border-radius:12px;box-shadow:0 2px 3px #24302903;color:var(--text-color,#243029);font:400 13px/1.5 var(--font,Roboto,sans-serif)}.ds-card-title{margin:0;padding:16px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color,#e0e6df);font-size:14px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.4}.ds-card-body{padding:12px 18px 16px}@media(max-width:640px){.ds-card-title{padding:15px}.ds-card-body{padding:10px 15px 14px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Device Catalog Selection",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "A selected device in the compact catalog, with exact MQTT identity and qualified status.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-device-row\" href=\"#device\"><strong>Имя устройства</strong><code>MQTT ID</code><span>Каналы не получены</span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-device-row{display:grid;gap:6px;padding:15px 16px;border-top:1px solid var(--border-color,#e0e6df);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--primary-color,#568d2d) 9%,var(--input-background,#fff));color:var(--text-color,#243029);font:400 13px/1.5 var(--font,Roboto,sans-serif);text-decoration:none;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-device-row strong{font-weight:500}.ds-device-row code{padding:0;background:none;color:var(--gray-color,#67736b);font:400 11px SFMono-Regular,Consolas,\"Liberation Mono\",monospace}.ds-device-row span{color:var(--gray-color,#67736b);font-size:12px;line-height:1.45}.ds-device-row:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--primary-color,#568d2d) 5%,var(--input-background,#fff));color:var(--text-color,#243029)}.ds-device-row:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--primary-color,#568d2d);outline-offset:-3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Technical Channel Disclosure",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "A keyboard-operable technical group kept below primary channel tasks.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-channel-group\"><summary><h3>Счётчики и служебные каналы</h3></summary><p>Служебные сведения устройства</p></details>",
      "css": ".ds-channel-group{color:var(--text-color,#243029);font:400 13px/1.5 var(--font,Roboto,sans-serif)}.ds-channel-group>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;padding:11px 0;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color,#e0e6df)}.ds-channel-group>summary::before{content:\"\";width:7px;height:7px;border-right:1px solid currentColor;border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;transform:rotate(-45deg);margin-right:3px}.ds-channel-group[open]>summary::before{transform:rotate(45deg)}.ds-channel-group h3{font-weight:500;font-size:14px;margin:0;line-height:1.5}.ds-channel-group>summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--primary-color,#568d2d);outline-offset:2px}.ds-channel-group>p{padding:11px 0;margin:0;color:var(--gray-color,#67736b)}@media(max-width:640px){.ds-channel-group h3{font-size:13px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Operate mode",
    "overview": "A restrained technical workspace for operating a controller. The original WB logo, Roboto, green actions and dark navigation carry the identity; pale green neutrals and white work surfaces organize dense information. Typography, borders and spacing establish hierarchy across the overview and native editors.\n\nThis records the implemented fork of homeui v2.208.1-wb100. It is an independent UI proposal. Its visual authority is the built application, including retained native widgets and editors, rather than a new decorative style for their contents.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Recognizable WB identity and technical terminology.",
      "Persistent dark navigation beside a light workspace.",
      "Quiet bordered surfaces, compact controls and readable telemetry.",
      "Shared treatment across AngularJS and React screens."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Theme Continuity Rule",
        "body": "New controls inherit the established semantic CSS variables and native state meanings.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Evidence in State Rule",
        "body": "Distinguish interface connection, received channel errors, missing data and configuration conflicts in text. Missing channels, an empty journal or the absence of reported errors does not establish physical device health. Preserve these distinctions in labels and empty states.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable History Rule",
        "body": "Preserve chart axes and summary text at (12px) at narrow widths. Reduce tick count when space is limited; do not shrink the labels with the plot. Use tabular numerals for readings and summaries.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Surface Rule",
        "body": "Use borders and tone for resting structure; reserve substantial shadow for floating menus and dialogs.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the original WB logo, Roboto and green identity.",
      "**Do** use semantic theme variables across new and native controls.",
      "**Do** retain visible focus, validation, disabled and connection states.",
      "**Do** keep readings tabular, units subordinate and chart axes readable on mobile.",
      "**Do** wrap toolbars and stack forms while preserving editor and table usability."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** replace the WB identity or recolor native SVG content to match the shell.",
      "**Don't** make destructive actions look like ordinary green actions.",
      "**Don't** hardcode light colors where existing semantic theme variables apply.",
      "**Don't** shrink chart labels with the plot or remove native status/error information.",
      "**Don't** add decorative elevation or motion absent from the implemented system."
    ]
  }
}
